      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int x{e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{e}^{5x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{5x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{25}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
