    "q-2426": {
      "dom_id": "step-q2426",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={sec}^{2}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ where $\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\int \\frac{1}{u}(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
