    "q-49680": {
      "dom_id": "step-q49680",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{1/2}4x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=4x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=4 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{4x} & ⇒ & v=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into  the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 4x\\cdot {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x. \\\\  & =x{e}^{4x}-\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}4x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={x{e}^{4x}|}_{0}^{1/2}-{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x{e}^{4x}|}_{0}^{1/2}-{\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x}|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4(1/2)}-0\\cdot {e}^{4\\cdot 0}]-\\frac{1}{4}[{e}^{4(1/2)}-{e}^{4\\cdot 0}] \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}-0]-\\frac{1}{4}[{e}^{2}-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
