    "q-349241": {
      "dom_id": "step-q349241",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\pi x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2\\pi x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=2\\pi  \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x) & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2\\pi x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\pi x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x))-\\int (-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x))\\cdot 2\\pi \\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\pi x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-2(1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 0))+\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 0)) \\\\  & =-2(-1-0)+\\frac{2}{\\pi }(0-0) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
