      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⇒ & v=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2(\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =2(0-0)+\\frac{2}{3}(-1-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
