    "q-49669": {
      "dom_id": "step-q49669",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into  the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi /6}+\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi /6}+{\\frac{2}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}[\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & +\\frac{2}{9}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}[0-0]+\\frac{2}{9}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-49669-a",
